 offensive accent  classic aliens in the star wars  franchise made you want to buy their  action figures the aliens and the  phantom menace largely reminded  moviegoers of ugly racial stereotypes  from earth but without any commentary to  justify their presence  after luke skywalker is rescued from the  clutches of hoth's cold weather at the  start of empire strikes back he's  talking to han solo and leia organa when  the discussion turns into an argument  between organa and solo concerning the  possibility of leia harboring secret  romantic attractions to the scoundrel to  prove that solo is wrong organa proceeds  to plant a big smooch on luke's lips  well i guess you don't know everything  about women yet  [Music]  in the grand scheme of star wars lore  it's apparent why this scene goes too  far given that skywalker and organa are  eventually revealed to be twins  separated at birth in defense of the  empire strikes back that piece of lore  wasn't defined yet when the film was in  production with george lucas initially  planning at one point to have luke's  sister be a new character still as part  of a sprawling saga the greater context  of the duo's relationship makes this  moment squirm inducing rather than its  initial intent of registering is just  humorous no wonder this kiss has been  burned into the minds of star wars fans  for all the wrong reasons  that was so wrong  throughout her screen time in solo a  star wars story l-337 is all about  giving droids autonomy and freeing them  from their human masters this passion  comes to a head on a kessel mine mission  where she leads a droid revolution just  before getting shot and killed in the  heat of the battle here it appears that  l3's storyline has come to an end but  solo isn't finished with this character  just yet shortly afterward el3's  consciousness is uploaded to the  millennium falcon a development l3 has  no say in and that all her previous  actions suggest she would be vehemently  against it's a c