 first act it isn't until the  action ships off the planet to tatooine  that she gets a new costume though leia  didn't don this bikini again in return  of the jedi this costume quickly became  an iconic piece of imagery that was  common in cosplay circles and  merchandising the latter use of the  chain bikini costume is downright  disturbing given how organa is kept on a  chain and forced to wear the skimpy  outfit by jabba the hutt however  lucasfilm merchandising had no problem  taking this image and putting it on  posters t-shirts and other items the  exploitation of leia and by extension  actress carrie fisher only ended when  disney bought the rights to star wars  and announced they were discontinuing  merchandise with a bikini outfit  a little more than halfway into the 2008  movie star wars the clone wars audiences  meet a new character in zero the hut  he's a crime lord like the much more  famous job of the hutt but there are a  few key differences between the two for  one thing zero speaks perfect english  for another he's got the voice of truman  capote and is covered in purple skin the  combination of a flamboyant voice and  the color purple which is often  associated with the lgbtqia plus  community makes it clear that zero the  huts is a gay stereotype of the sort  that belongs in hollywood's past not  present there's nothing inherently wrong  with having a villain character who's  incidentally gay but it is strange to  lean on such broad queer stereotypes as  a way of defining your antagonist this  becomes even more recognizable and  franchised as devoid of nuanced queer  representation of star wars it also  doesn't help that zero's character  traits stemming from queer stereotypes  feel like they exist to make  heterosexual viewers giggle out of  mockery while he may be one of the brand  new characters introduced in the star  wars the clone wars feature zero is also  an unfortunate relic of when  flamboyantly evil queer villains were  common in child