acter die to  motivate the story's male protagonist  this tiresome narrative staple feels  especially out of place in a star wars  movie given how often this franchise has  been all about subverting expectations  rather than giving in to them the lack  of many other black women in star wars  also makes this death extra  disappointing even actress tandy way  newton who played val commented on this  in an interview about solo now could  have been a landmark star wars character  but instead she was a disappointing  example of how little noticed black  women get in this franchise  everybody loves grogu aka baby yoda fans  make memes about him t-shirts featuring  his adorable mug are everywhere he's  even gotten his own macy's thanksgiving  day parade float however that doesn't  mean grosgu is devoid of controversy in  the star wars franchise one season two  episode of the mandalorian features  grosgrou scarfing down the eggs of their  frog-like alien passenger while the  titular lead of the mandalorian tells  groggu to knock it off this baby is  always eyeballing the canister  containing the eggs that is a dark gag  fans did not respond well to grogu's egg  consumption which in effect reduces the  population of this already struggling  alien species to even lower numbers he's  eating their children a brief backlash  occurred that proved so loud that a  creative arts manager at lucasfilm had  to put out a response defending grogu's  actions by comparing the frog eggs to  chicken eggs of course the controversy  didn't last long and people were soon  back to making adorable gifts however  this character's controversial approach  to satisfying his hunger shows that any  star wars character even fan favorites  can end up going too far check out one  of our newest videos right here plus  even more looper videos about star wars  are coming soon subscribe to our youtube  channel and hit the bell so you don't  miss a single one  [Music]

